  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q14",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Solve the equation $e^x+e^{-x}=2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=0$.",
      "worked": "Multiply both sides by $e^x$, which is positive for all real $x$, then factorise.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\ne^x+e^{-x}&=2\\\\\ne^{2x}+1&=2e^x\\\\\ne^{2x}-2e^x+1&=0\\\\\n(e^x-1)^2&=0\\\\\ne^x&=1\\\\\nx&=0\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 31
  },
